  "final_text": "**Proposed disposition:** CLOSE_FP, confidence 0.8. The proposal is recorded and awaits a human decision.\n\n**Three facts that drove it:**\n1. The BUY of 18,930 (7.9x depth) at 9997 was cancelled after 803 ms. It had no fills, and the trader made no opposite-side trade. So there was no benefit (feature b), no price move, no repetition in the session, and no prior alerts.\n2. The trader entered a BUY of 1,893 at the same price 1.2 s after the cancel. That is exactly one tenth of the first order, which points to an extra digit that was then corrected. This is the fat-finger explanation, and I judged it supported.\n3. The trader is a prop trader with no registered market-making instruments and a typical order size of 500. There were no market events or risk events, so market making, event reaction and risk cancellation are ruled out.\n\n**What would change my mind:** a sell-side trade around 15:53:42\u201343, a repeat of the cycle later in the session, or evidence that the 1,893 order was not a correction of the first.",
